{
 "task": "HND-XACT-06",
 "source": "Refresh-selected genuine Microsoft XACT3.6 x86 and x64, hnd06-<group> cells (PROVENANCE.json)",
 "rule": [
  "Every play-wave family (1 PlayWave, 3 PlayWaveTrackVariation, 4 PlayWaveEffectVariation, 6 PlayWaveTrackEffectVariation) plays a raw loop byte n (0..5, 100, 254 measured) n+1 times; XACT_TRACK_PROPERTIES report loopCount n.",
  "Only track NEW_ON_LOOP (variation bit 22, families 3 and 6) makes each pass a separate complete wave (n+1 PREPARED/PLAY/STOP/DESTROY), each the next candidate: ordered A0,A1,..., random drawn with repeats, shuffle alternating its two candidates.",
  "Without track NEW_ON_LOOP one wave of the first drawn candidate is held for all passes, whatever the variation type and whatever the effect NEW_ON_LOOP bits (Pitch Variation New Variation On Loop, effect flags 0x0100).",
  "A held wave with a loop region plays prefix + (n+1) x region + suffix; separate NEW_ON_LOOP waves each play the whole wave once. The track duration property is wave length + n x region length in both cases.",
  "With the pitch NEW_ON_LOOP the held wave's 101-pass hold barely varies between runs, unlike a held wave without it: its pitch varies over the passes (statistical, from holds; no PCM)."
 ],
 "measured_on": [
  "event types 1, 3, 4 and 6; ordered, random and shuffle track variations with two weight-255 candidates in one resident bank",
  "raw loop bytes 0..4 (effect, region), 1 and 3 (random/shuffle), 5, 100, 254 (ordered with and without NEW_ON_LOOP), 100 (pitch)",
  "one-second 22050 Hz waves, without and with a smpl loop region [5512, 16537]; Pitch Variation -100..100 cents, Operator 0",
  "x86 and x64, lookahead 250 ms; every group reran the retained TQ-XACT-31, one-wave resident and HND-XACT-02 samebank controls"
 ],
 "not_measured": [
  "volume and filter effect NEW_ON_LOOP bits, effect ADD operators, type 6 with both track and effect NEW_ON_LOOP",
  "the per-pass pitch values or when within a pass they change (no PCM)",
  "Ordered From Random and Random No Immediate Repeats, more than two candidates, non-uniform weights",
  "raw byte 255 (CNA keeps the owner policy), streaming banks, cross-bank candidates, Microsoft PCM/gain"
 ],
 "pass_unit": "a pass is one hold of the same matrix and architecture's one-wave resident control (about 660-700 ms under Wine's XAudio2, start/stop latency included); a region hold is reported in half passes; the 101- and 255-pass holds of nol0 are read with the held-pass length of the same architecture's 6-pass nol0/raw5 hold (666.7 ms)",
 "pitch_per_pass": {
  "spread_limit_ms": 20.0,
  "method": "mean pass = the single held wave's WAVEPLAY..WAVESTOP hold / 101; the spread is over x86/x64 x three repeats",
